{
  "id": "COMPOUND:4287 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "Tricarballylic acid appears to have a potential relationship with A2780cisR through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Tricarballylic acid acts as a target for MOVP-3 and 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide, both of which are targets of Neridienone A, which in turn targets A2780cisR. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions that could contribute to the observed effect on A2780cisR. The presence of multiple targets in this pathway, including both MOVP-3 and CCRF-HSB-2, suggests that Tricarballylic acid may influence cellular processes through different mechanisms, potentially involving receptor activation or enzyme inhibition. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Tricarballylic acid possibly modulating cellular functions through a network of targets that ultimately affect A2780cisR. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but further validation through direct interaction studies or in vivo experiments would be necessary to confirm the precise role of Tricarballylic acid in this context.",
